{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01178",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.76,
      "end_seconds": 6.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Doctor, hi, where would you like me to put my coat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.79,
      "end_seconds": 12.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "Yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 14.26,
      "end_seconds": 21.64,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "Good afternoon, uh, doctor. I look after them so I thought I'd come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.41,
      "end_seconds": 26.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Please do. Extra information is always welcome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.27,
      "end_seconds": 30.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "I'm here because of nausea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.27,
      "end_seconds": 36.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Okay, what's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.6,
      "end_seconds": 47.68,
      "duration_seconds": 10.08,
      "text": "Hm. It was either the end of last month or earlier than that. I couldn't tell you the date."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.86,
      "end_seconds": 57.76,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.64,
      "end_seconds": 68.38,
      "duration_seconds": 9.74,
      "text": "It happens all the time. Pretty mild, if I'm being honest. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.12,
      "end_seconds": 71.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.23,
      "end_seconds": 79.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.29,
      "text": "Um, it usually comes with cramping tummy pain. I've also been feeling dehydrated."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.2,
      "end_seconds": 89.41,
      "duration_seconds": 9.21,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.84,
      "end_seconds": 107.54,
      "duration_seconds": 16.7,
      "text": "I get some relief from drinking water. Mostly severe. I didn't want to bother you but it keeps coming back. Yeah, with cramping tummy pain, it's a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.74,
      "end_seconds": 112.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "What about a low fever, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.01,
      "end_seconds": 123.31,
      "duration_seconds": 9.3,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, five days. With low fever, about a four out of ten. Honestly, all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.23,
      "end_seconds": 129.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any confusion, dizziness or vomiting blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.74,
      "end_seconds": 134.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "No, uh, no confusion, dizziness or vomiting blood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.94,
      "end_seconds": 141.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "What about black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.35,
      "end_seconds": 147.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "Right, no, I haven't had any black stools."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.03,
      "end_seconds": 151.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.73,
      "end_seconds": 154.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "No changes there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.2,
      "end_seconds": 158.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 164.3,
      "end_seconds": 178.79,
      "duration_seconds": 14.49,
      "text": "She is on escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day for the anxiety, I give it to her. Sorry, what was I saying, it's mirtazapine, at night for my mood, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.21,
      "end_seconds": 182.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 184.19,
      "end_seconds": 191.9,
      "duration_seconds": 7.71,
      "text": "It's 15 milligrams. She is on ORS, after each loose stool, I give it to her."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.29,
      "end_seconds": 211.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.04,
      "end_seconds": 229.47,
      "duration_seconds": 16.43,
      "text": "Well, I've had high blood pressure for five years now. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. My neighbour said I should get it looked at. I've had anxiety for about ten years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.46,
      "end_seconds": 231.39,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "Right, right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.29,
      "end_seconds": 237.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "I've had depression for two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.11,
      "end_seconds": 241.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Okay, and besides that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.97,
      "end_seconds": 247.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "Okay, I can see high blood pressure and depression in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.71,
      "end_seconds": 265.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.09,
      "end_seconds": 269.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "I've, I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 270.95,
      "end_seconds": 278.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.77,
      "text": "Actually, I remember she had some kind of reaction to naproxen before. I couldn't swear to it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.09,
      "end_seconds": 282.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Really? I don't think so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.0,
      "end_seconds": 288.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "Fair enough, I'll write down both versions. Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 289.94,
      "end_seconds": 292.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Ah, no, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.25,
      "end_seconds": 298.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.88,
      "end_seconds": 311.58,
      "duration_seconds": 12.7,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette. I do a yoga class on Thursdays. I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.31,
      "end_seconds": 317.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.54,
      "end_seconds": 321.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.46,
      "end_seconds": 342.85,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "Your mouth is a bit dry and your tummy is soft with mild tenderness all over."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.38,
      "end_seconds": 347.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "You can sit up now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.85,
      "end_seconds": 376.8,
      "duration_seconds": 14.95,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, I'd lean towards infective gastroenteritis, likely after recent travel. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. It could also be food poisoning, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.46,
      "end_seconds": 381.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 383.1,
      "end_seconds": 406.62,
      "duration_seconds": 23.52,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with infective gastroenteritis, likely after recent travel do well once it's treated properly. Let's get a stool test, for diarrhoea. Let's get blood tests, for dehydration. Small sips often are better than large drinks, and eat plain food as soon as you can. Let's plan a check after the stool result."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 407.74,
      "end_seconds": 411.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Right, uh, okay, I'll arrange it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 412.84,
      "end_seconds": 415.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Okay, that's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 416.59,
      "end_seconds": 419.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Um, thank you, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
}